# .trivyignore — Trivy CVE exceptions
# Format: one CVE/GHSA ID per line (optionally with expiry: id exp:YYYY-MM-DD)
#
# HOW TO USE:
#   trivy image --ignorefile .trivyignore <image>
#
# POLICY: Only add an entry here when the vulnerable code is:
#   (a) vendored INSIDE a tool (not callable from app code), AND
#   (b) a fixed package version is already installed in site-packages
#
# Review and remove entries as upstream packages ship fixes.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# jaraco.context — vendored inside setuptools/_vendor/jaraco/
# The app never calls jaraco.context directly; it is only used internally
# by setuptools during package management operations (not at runtime).
# Fixed version (6.1.0) is installed in site-packages.
# CVE: https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-23949
CVE-2026-23949

# wheel — METADATA found inside pip/setuptools bundled .whl archives.
# wheel is a build tool; it is not imported or used at application runtime.
# Fixed version (0.46.2) is installed in site-packages.
# CVE: https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-24049
CVE-2026-24049
